L.append("- **GAP-061** (the self-hosted runner) gates **GAP-093** (Gate 6's threshold\n  enforcement) and is itself waited on by nothing else open.")
L.append("- **GAP-045** (scenario replay through the live pipeline) gates **GAP-087** (PN-16,\n  the planning panel), already in progress on the rest of its scope.")
L.append("- **GAP-023** (data loaders) no longer gates **GAP-024** (GPU point-cloud\n  registration), as of 2026-09-08: GAP-023's remaining item is the DEM half, a\n  projection library that is an owner decision, and the LAS and bounded-COPC readers\n  GAP-024 needs are built and fixture-tested. GAP-024's CPU reference is built and\n  gated, its runner is registered as of the same day, and its §2 verification row\n  uses synthetic clouds, so nothing blocks the WGSL work. **GAP-098** (nothing loads\n  or draws a point cloud) is deliberately not an edge to it: GAP-024 makes the engine\n  correct, GAP-098 makes it reachable, and either can be built first.")
L.append("- **GAP-077**, **GAP-078**, and **GAP-079** (in progress) all feed **GAP-080** (the\n  first two trained models); none of the three has a gap of its own blocking it.")
L.append("- **GAP-067** (this table's own walk) is blocked on nothing: D-16 and D-10, its two\n  named decisions, are both Resolved. It is now purely a matter of the owner's time\n  against 43 rows, not a dependency.")
L.append("\n## Counts\n")
L.append("| Increment | Gaps | Closed / In progress / Open / Planned | Effort S / M / L / XL |")
L.append("|---|---|---|---|")
for inc in ["I2", "I3", "I4"]:
    rows = [g for g in G if g["target"] == inc]
    ec = Counter(g["effort"] for g in rows)
    # A gap's status is its last history entry, so this is how far the increment has
